@Dan
I recognise 11/08/2026 as a representation of  August 11, 2026. In the US it would be 08/11/2026. Would you prefer 11\08\2026? That looks odd to me.
I usually write the year in 4 digits to  reduce the ambiguity of 08/11/26. And of course others may break up the digits with marks like  - or .

@Joe Horton

Speaking of lookups, I've never figured out what's considered "fair". I try not to do lookups at all, unless I'm stuck for a long time right near the end. The most I ever do is one or two; rarely three. But most days I try to finish with no lookups. I guess my question is, is your streak considered tainted if you look something up?

I know there's no right answer!

