Also, a nickname here is not related to your actual name, it's a name adopted, or foisted on you that refers to something you did or how you look, and some families always do it, some not. I've known Bumper, (falling over a lot when a toddler) Pipsqueak, (squeaky voice when young) Nibby (His Nibs), Bee (father said she looked like a little bird when born, which became B) Nebby (inquisitive and nosy), Boulder (boy with a big head). I never did it, but some people do.

