@Team Live I think they are cracking down on folks sharing an account, like the streaming services, to charge more. 

Though supporting journalism is important to us, I have “rationalized” our choice not to do that for many reasons. Most importantly, my husband and I share the NYT account since if we chose the printed paper option, we would, of course, both read the same paper. Fortunately or unfortunately for me, he has no interest in puzzles but will appreciatively listen to my word obsessions. Congrats to you two for doing this together! Someone once posted about he and his partner screen mirroring the Sunday puzzle to share via TV screen and I thought that was so cool! Daily on an app is ambitious. 🥰

As far as streaming goes, the two of us are often in different cities, and we are constantly having to verify our info. We have to [gasp] call HULU on the regular. So good luck with the NYT folks answering!

